irst impression was wrong.\n\u003e \n\u003e \u003e (e.g. use of `normpath` inside),\n\u003e \n\u003e In the above commit I probably should have replaced the block that contains `normpath` with use of `rev_resolve_path`.\n\nI agree.\n\n\u003e \u003e i.e. transition it to use pathlib.\n\u003e \n\u003e That doesn't seem necessary for following the new path handling conventions.\n\nTrue, there are more important things to be done ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1567837786,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUyOTA3ODg2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3643#issuecomment-529078863"},"message":"I think it is fine to close this issue at this point. Thx for the input.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1567837786,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjYxNjAzNTU2MQ=="},"status":2}]}